{"title":"1986 USAMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two distinct circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/3101a8fb302472d167884ef2296671d5ded79da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7a629a3ef8f8f46f7850ebdeac02d4b52bad2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> are drawn in the plane. They intersect at points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> is the diameter of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/3101a8fb302472d167884ef2296671d5ded79da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" />. A point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7a629a3ef8f8f46f7850ebdeac02d4b52bad2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> and inside <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/3101a8fb302472d167884ef2296671d5ded79da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> is also given.\n</p><p>Using only a \"T-square\" (i.e. an instrument which can produce a straight line joining two points and the perpendicular to a line through a point on or off the line), find a construction for two points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/3101a8fb302472d167884ef2296671d5ded79da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> is perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/d/9ad3c8b51037d6169d6fcaa2bfb2209b18516477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CPD$\" width=\"56\" height=\"12\" /> is a right angle.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Extend line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3bb4eeb347e74e025fd175c22f1f7275af0555e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> to meet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/3101a8fb302472d167884ef2296671d5ded79da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />. Draw perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and let it intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/3101a8fb302472d167884ef2296671d5ded79da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff9d2add1273f7f294d4f0318b0ed4340c07768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> denote the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> onto <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/8/e78e4ccd43190129634f2667dce5e18f135e68c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;=AN \\cap \\ell_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"110\" height=\"19\" /> (Note that: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/9/c2956e3e61d36a8570058ac2f2c0d597a1284244.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P, P&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"19\" /> are reflections of each other with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />). Draw a line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/970a3f7a0a3b548d0684d391994a6366f8d71ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/f/3ff9d2add1273f7f294d4f0318b0ed4340c07768.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/4/3545551b3d62c4e23d5df7352a55602d0aa9adcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P&#39;$\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/970a3f7a0a3b548d0684d391994a6366f8d71ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> intersect <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/7/2a7a629a3ef8f8f46f7850ebdeac02d4b52bad2b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/6/b267383fc4f3f4ca65df94834860e1e2468dab1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A, Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> are on the same side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/970a3f7a0a3b548d0684d391994a6366f8d71ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/3/d23cf5b5064e55b8d027f597a6f8e29f7e26b576.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = PZ \\cap AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"119\" height=\"14\" />. Draw a line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/7/587edad44bc07186584e2522b8fe2769515b4065.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ell_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"15\" /> perpendicular to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> meeting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/0/3101a8fb302472d167884ef2296671d5ded79da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"21\" height=\"15\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/7/1375da8b94d688b4928311f04d35a57081ee0f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C, D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" />. We claim we found points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/7/1375da8b94d688b4928311f04d35a57081ee0f1e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C, D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"36\" height=\"16\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/6198aafcfcd5eae34fef18bd1cac46ffc9fd207e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CPD = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p>We will prove that the construction works: \n</p><p>Note that: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/9/c2956e3e61d36a8570058ac2f2c0d597a1284244.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P, P&#39;$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"41\" height=\"19\" /> are reflections of each other with respect to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Thus: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/2/8f2e590510ae25e49c6337e67242299502ec63ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P, P&#39;, Z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"19\" /> have same perpendicular distance from line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />. Note: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/c/dacbc739d92f83aa1d2fd48fe58a5e27400cdd90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$PX=XZ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"87\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/d/14d9168117e2b9fa672c0ef012db9fe40729c606.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XC=XD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"89\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Due to Power of Point: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/d/4dd9bca7c7d56c04391de0871c0d855832ddb917.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PX^2 = PX \\cdot XZ = AX \\cdot XB = CX \\cdot XD = XC^2.\\]\" width=\"401\" height=\"15\" /> Thus: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/e/75e54d81f5665ff1552b1dbc9f7e22875fc006c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$XP=XC=XD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"144\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/5/09593ae95161cc114be56c247a029bbbf8bc7c4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X, C, D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> are collinear. Thus: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> lies on the circle with diameter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/6198aafcfcd5eae34fef18bd1cac46ffc9fd207e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CPD = 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"109\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_USAMO\" title=\"1986 USAMO\">1986 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"1986 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=1986\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1986 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1986 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1986 USAMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1986 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1986 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1986_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1986 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017022757\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.031 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.054 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 322/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1267/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 9741/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   11.801      1 -total\n 56.39%    6.654      1 Template:USAMO_box\n 41.83%    4.937      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:15080:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017022757 and revision id